    <string name="reception_hint">Reception LED from RSRP/RSRQ: green above −95 dBm, yellow −105 to −95 dBm, red below −105 dBm or RSRQ below −18 dB. RSRP at or below −125 dBm triggers the no-signal tone. Alert tones follow the same signal rules.</string>
    <string name="geiger_hint">Clicks speed up when RTT, jitter, or packet loss worsen. Low-signal clicks follow RSRP/RSRQ tiers (5 s / 2.5 s / 1 s / 0.5 s). Limited service uses a two-tone alert, or 300 ms on/off on 2G with no home GSM. No signal is pulsed unless you are completely out of service with no SOS on any SIM — then it stays continuous.</string>
